plusUnwrapT -- SEQ 399 (Tony, 2026-10-22): A DATED EXCEPTION TO THE STAR LAW. opAddAttribute's list arm unwraps each
list entry that is a holder, one level, before attaching it; a non-holder entry attaches as before. So `pb +% hOp hTgt
hArg;` attaches the three holders' CONTENTS (nOp=1 nTgt=2 nArg=3) -- what three `+%` lines of `*h` attach. Rows:
pb all holders; pm a mixed list (one holder, two plain fields); pe a holder of a DATA-LESS field (the empty holder that
can exist) and a plain field; pn a field bound by `:=` to NOTHING -- which leaves it a plain field, not a holder
(isGrouP 0, measured), so it attaches as itself on both sides of the exception. Before SEQ 399: pb hOp=nOp hTgt=nTgt
hArg=nArg; pm hOp=nOp nTgt=2 nArg=3; pe hDataless=nEmpty nArg=3; pn hNull nArg=3.
